import { FilesystemReaderCopy } from "../model"

pub fn copy -> FilesystemReaderCopy = FilesystemReaderCopy {
  summary: "A value carrying the failed file operation, target Path, reason, and related details for a useful error report.",
  taskTitle: "Explain why saving failed",
  purpose: "Create a new report, then try creating another file with the same name. Instead of merely saying “save failed,” read FileSystemError to explain which operation failed, at which path, and for what reason.",
  setup: "The imported fs handles file operations, paths handles paths, and effects composes work. fn describe error: fs.FileSystemError -> file: paths.Path -> String takes error and file and returns a String. Access fields with . as in error.kind. let names immutable values within the block, and the final string is its return value.",
  after: [
    "FileSystemError.operation identifies the failed operation, path the target, and kind the reason. Here they are WriteFile, the Path for report.txt, and FileAlreadyExists. The actual temporary directory name varies, so paths.render converts file and error.path to strings and == compares them, displaying True.",
    "otherPath holds a second path when one is relevant, such as a move destination. Its type Maybe<Path> has two shapes: Nothing for no value and Just other for a present value. match selects the corresponding branch. This write has Nothing, so the description uses none. show converts operation and reason values to text; ${...} inserts that text into the description.",
    "effect fn report defines work taking directory as a Path and producing String when run. with FileSystem names the required service; fails ReportError names failures. |> passes Left or Right from paths.child into effects.fromEither to make work, and file <- receives the Path. do runs operations in order; _ <- waits for a write without keeping its result.",
    "effects.attempt executes the second write. An ordinary failure becomes Left error and success becomes Right. The failed match branch calls describe error file. ReportError’s PathFailure, WriteFailure, and ReadFailure retain problems from the other stages, wrapped with mapError. deriving Show enables their display.",
    "The description includes original read back from disk, and effects.succeed returns it as a successful value. main uses withTemporaryDirectory to provide a dedicated workspace and remove it afterward. The outer attempt and match choose message, which println displays."
  ],
  details: [
    "This is an ordinary failure value whose fields the caller can inspect, not a JS exception class. effects.attempt captures that failure as a value; it does not convert every unexpected runtime problem or cancellation into a FileSystemError.",
    "Other kinds include FileNotFound and PermissionDenied. Do not conclude that every failure is FileAlreadyExists from this duplicate-creation example. Reading operation separately from kind distinguishes a read from a write even when the reason is the same.",
    "An invalid path string produces PathError before file access. readTextUtf8 wraps access problems in FileAccessFailure and distinguishes malformed UTF-8 with FileUtf8Failure. FileSystemError alone does not represent a text-decoding problem."
  ],
  comparisonBefore: "TS can inspect a value received by try/catch and read Node fields such as code and path. A caught value is not guaranteed to have those fields, so checks depend on the use case.",
  comparisonAfter: "Here FileSystemError has declared field names and types, letting the caller read the operation, path, and reason directly. Reports need not depend only on OS-specific message text. The caller still decides how to respond."
}
